"text":"When to emit the gathered elements; its ","type":"text"},{"code":"Element","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sequence’s, inferred from the call.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"strategy"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"return-value","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Return Value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A sequence of the upstream’s elements, in order, in arrays of one or more.","type":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The strategy decides when the pending elements are flushed: every so many elements","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/count(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), every interval","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/time(interval:clock:tolerance:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), on a signal or a unit of work","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SignalBatchStrategy","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), whenever any of several does","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/either(_:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), or by a rule of your own (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"). After every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"flush, each strategy starts over. A flush with nothing pending emits nothing; the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sequence never emits an empty array.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When the upstream finishes, the pending elements, if any, are emitted as a last array and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the sequence finishes. When the upstream throws, the pending elements are dropped and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sequence throws the same error. A signal that finishes stops firing while the batches go","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on; a signal that throws ends the sequence with its error.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The upstream and the strategy run in tasks of their own, started when iteration begins,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so the upstream is read ahead of the consumer, and arrays the consumer hasn’t taken yet"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are buffered. Cancelling the consumer, or dropping its iterator, cancels both. An"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"upstream or signal that ignores cancellation keeps the internal task alive until its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pending "},{"code":"next()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" returns, and is not read again after that; the batched sequence itself"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ends at once."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Batching needs iOS 16, Mac Catalyst 16, macOS 13, tvOS 16, watchOS 9 or visionOS 1."}]},{"anchor":"Example","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Example"},{"code":["for try await batch in [1, 2, 3, 4].async.batch(strategy: .either(.count(3), .time(interval: .seconds(1), clock: ContinuousClock()))) {","    print(batch) \/\/ Prints [1, 2, 3], then [4]","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"name":"Throws","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Any error the upstream 